[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187256824","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118174#issuecomment-4187256824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118174","id":4187256824,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lHf4","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T15:13:56Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T15:14:15Z","body":"Based on past experiences/issues, it helps a lot to get the name of the active input and output device","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187256824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187328059","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118174#issuecomment-4187328059","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118174","id":4187328059,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lY47","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:05:59Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T16:05:59Z","body":"> Based on past experiences/issues, it helps a lot to get the name of the active input and output device\r\n\r\nI talk about that in the proposal. Do you know of any way to get the explicit name of the active input/output devices? Getting them with smth like `get_output_device()` only returns `\"Default\"`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187328059/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187359114","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118174#issuecomment-4187359114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118174","id":4187359114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lgeK","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:28:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T16:31:05Z","body":"Note: For input devices, `Audio > Driver > Enable Input` must be enabled in project settings.  \r\nThough it never prints anything in my case.  \r\nAnd I also only ever get the `Default` output device.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# my device\r\nUbuntu 24.04.4 LTS 24.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n# example code\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tprint(\"out\")\r\n\tprint(AudioServer.get_output_device_list())\r\n\t#print(AudioServer.get_output_device())\r\n\tprint(\"in\")\r\n\tprint(AudioServer.get_input_device_list())\r\n\t#print(AudioServer.get_input_device())\r\n```\r\n\r\nEven if I change my input/output to yeti on my computer, godot won't notice. But you can get the devices. Though you'll need to filter out the useless ones using some hardcoded \"disallow-list\" (here `pci` is a dead giveaway; this practice is, sadly, not uncommon for hardware info):\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# output\r\n# added linebreaks for readability\r\nout\r\n[\"Default\",\r\n\"alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3-platform-skl_hda_dsp_generic.HiFi__hw_sofhdadsp_5__sink\",\r\n\"alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3-platform-skl_hda_dsp_generic.HiFi__hw_sofhdadsp_4__sink\",\r\n\"alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3-platform-skl_hda_dsp_generic.HiFi__hw_sofhdadsp_3__sink\",\r\n\"alsa_output.pci-0000_00_1f.3-platform-skl_hda_dsp_generic.HiFi__hw_sofhdadsp__sink\",\r\n\"alsa_output.usb-Blue_Microphones_Yeti_Stereo_Microphone_REV8-00.analog-stereo\"]\r\nin\r\n[\"Default\",\r\n\"alsa_input.pci-0000_00_1f.3-platform-skl_hda_dsp_generic.HiFi__hw_sofhdadsp__source\",\r\n\"alsa_input.pci-0000_00_1f.3-platform-skl_hda_dsp_generic.HiFi__hw_sofhdadsp_6__source\",\r\n\"alsa_input.usb-Blue_Microphones_Yeti_Stereo_Microphone_REV8-00.analog-stereo.3\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**If you have bluetooth device(s), maybe we can find out how they're connected. Here we see `USB`**  \r\nBluetooth is a pain for many issues in audio","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187359114/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187391722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118174#issuecomment-4187391722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118174","id":4187391722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lobq","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:46:43Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T16:46:43Z","body":"I thought of returning the lists, but it's too much. Filtering them perhaps is an option, but I don't know the best way to approach it, and is probably best handled on a case-by-case basis. Trying to get the explict name of the current device in code seems overkill too. Maybe best to wait an implementation of that in the AudioServer, since you'd probably need to make that work with multiple drivers.\r\nUntil there's some consensus, we should probably keep as is, unless there's an easy way around that I'm not seeing... I'd love this to have device information.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187391722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187404324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118174#issuecomment-4187404324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118174","id":4187404324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75lrgk","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-04T16:55:44Z","updated_at":"2026-04-04T17:30:05Z","body":"Yes, a straightforward answer is quite hard to get from the computer. And it will depend on platform and potentially even the driver.\r\n\r\n~~The simplest thing you can do right now is to check whether input/output device is **not empty** and **!= `Default`**.  \r\nIf it is just the default, print sth. like `Audio Input/Output: Default`.  \r\nIf a godot user set a valid input device manually via code, it should be a different value, then you could print e.g. `Audio Input: [whatever valid name the user entered]; Audio Output: Default`  \r\nor sth. along the line.~~\r\n\r\n**EDIT**: It slipped my mind: even if a user sets it via code, the editor won't pick up on it when you click that button…  \r\nTherefore, the above won't bring any merit until godot can give us info about the current device…","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187404324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4246045681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118174#issuecomment-4246045681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118174","id":4246045681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79FYPx","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"